# world-sea

Slice 2 of the plan after the walking skeleton: the §3 sea of `docs/spec.md`. It covers a Tiled-authored map with four small islands, shoals and docks, integer sailing with acceleration, braking and turning, docking, and a sight radius enforced per client on the server (§16), plus the client's map, camera and fogged minimap. It runs in parallel with `duel-core` and never touches that feature's paths.

- `feature.json`: one lane (`world`), the bundled reviewers, `prd` = `docs/spec.md`.
- `policy.json`: owned paths and five checks, with browser scenarios `join-private-match`, `two-ships-sync`, `sail-and-dock` and `out-of-sight`.
- `world-task.md`: the lane's outcome brief.
- `decisions.md`: the operator's decisions.

Launch from its own checkout (a `git worktree` of this repository, so it doesn't share a source checkout with `duel-core`): `workflow launch world-sea --dry-run`, then the launch line in `CLAUDE.md`.
{
  "version": "2.2.0",
  "name": "The \u00a73 sea: a tile map with islands, shoals and docks, sailing with acceleration, braking and turning, and a server-enforced sight radius (\u00a716)",
  "branch_prefix": "feature/world-sea",
  "prd": "docs/spec.md",
  "policy": "policy.json",
  "workers": [
    {
      "node_id": "world",
      "task": "world-task.md"
    }
  ],
  "reviewers": [
    {
      "reviewer_id": "general",
      "prompt": "builtin:general"
    },
    {
      "reviewer_id": "coverage",
      "prompt": "builtin:coverage"
    }
  ]
}
            {
              "id": "join-private-match",
              "description": "One browser creates a private match from the landing page; the HUD shows the code, the protocol version, one player and a connected status."
            },
            {
              "id": "two-ships-sync",
              "description": "Two browsers join the same private match with their ships in sight of each other; one sails with the keyboard and the other browser's view shows that ship at the new server-authoritative position."
            },
            {
              "id": "sail-and-dock",
              "description": "A browser sails its ship around a shoal to an island dock with the keyboard and docks there; the HUD shows the dock and the ship stops at it."
            },
            {
              "id": "out-of-sight",
              "description": "Two browsers in one match with their ships out of sight of each other: neither view lists or draws the other ship until one sails within the sight radius, and it disappears again when it sails away."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

